#
# Competency question: "For the closed-form signed-radial-field scene, what operator
# tree does the field's defining expression T(x) = A·x⁻ᵖ − B·(1−x)⁻q + C recover?"
# This exercises that the exact form is stored as a structured AST, not an opaque
# string: following math:argumentSlot/math:slotExpression from the body to arbitrary
# depth reaches every math:ApplicationExpression node, and each reports its
# math:operator. Over examples/signed-radial-field-closed-form.ttl the answer is
# exactly the nine operator nodes — the root Addition, the outer Subtraction, the two
# Multiplications (A·x⁻ᵖ and B·(1−x)⁻q), the two Exponentiations (x⁻ᵖ and (1−x)⁻q),
# the inner Subtraction (1−x), and the two Negations (−p and −q) — so the operand
# structure of the signed compactified curve is recovered node by node.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX ex:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/radial-cf/>

SELECT ?node ?operator WHERE {
    ex:signedRadialFieldCF math:definingExpression ?root .
    ?root (math:argumentSlot/math:slotExpression)* ?node .
    ?node a math:ApplicationExpression ;
          math:operator ?operator .
}
ORDER BY ?node
